2026-10-13 — Added a Galley-only Reviewer decision form to the existing defect detail workflow.

Implementation: The existing review decision endpoint now accepts only APPROVE or REJECT, an optional maintenance-team UUID, and an optional remark of at most 2000 characters. New backend decision options return only active tenant maintenance teams with an active member authorized for PERFORM_ACTION. Both options and decision submission require REVIEW permission and membership in the defect's currently routed Reviewer team. Decision writes lock the defect row, enforce GALLEY and reviewable statuses, reject repeat decisions until correction is submitted, and validate the selected maintenance team again. Approval moves a case to INSPECTION_REQUIRED and records its selected maintenance team in the append-only REVIEW_APPROVED event; the existing inspection-pass path remains responsible for creating the corrective action. Rejection creates REVIEW_REJECTED and creates no maintenance action. The rejected case remains REPORTED to permit reporting correction. A subsequent eligible Galley report submission updates the existing typed defect columns, appends another immutable typed form submission and REPORT_CORRECTED event, and returns the case to UNDER_REVIEW without replacing historical submissions. Reviewer detail displays the exact submitted form version and typed snapshot, with evidence fetched and downloaded through authorized endpoints.

