2026-10-14 — Configurable Galley Reviewer Decision form

Implemented the Galley Reviewer Decision configuration as a versioned Form Master workflow form. The existing Galley Area `DEFECT_REPORT` / `INITIAL_REPORT` publication and historical submissions are unchanged. The current backend has no `REVIEWER` stage enum; Form Master and resolution use the actual `REPORTED` and `UNDER_REVIEW` stages. A new published Reviewer version must contain exactly four approved bindings: required Decision, required Assign Team conditioned on `APPROVE`, required Rejection Reason (maximum 2,000 characters) conditioned on `REJECT`, and optional Remark (maximum 2,000 characters). Typed `{fieldKey, equals}` visibility configuration is validated at publication and again during server-side form resolution and decision submission.

The decision endpoint keeps its typed request contract (`decision`, optional `maintenanceTeamId`, optional `rejectionReason`, optional `remark`, exact `formId` and `versionId`). It requires a nonblank reason for REJECT, rejects team assignment on REJECT, requires an eligible active same-tenant Maintenance team on APPROVE, rechecks the exact current published configuration and routed Reviewer access, and records the decision details in the append-only event. Approval continues to `INSPECTION_REQUIRED`; maintenance assignment is still created only after inspection passes. The frontend renders configured field order/labels, loads team options only for APPROVE, and clears team/reason values when switching decisions.

The opt-in seed now creates a `LOCAL_DEMO_GALLEY_REVIEW_DECISION` draft only for the synthetic demo tenant when no Galley Reviewer Decision form already exists. The smoke-test seed path publishes that draft using `OperationalFormService`; it does not insert a published version or update administrator-owned forms. No Flyway migration was added because existing versioned form configuration and defect event storage support the feature.

