2026-10-14 — Implemented configurable Galley Closure Review

Implemented the closure-review stage using the existing operational-form versioning, workflow APIs, defect event history, attachment authorization, and tenant/team permission model. The form is a Form Master configuration (`CLOSURE_APPROVAL / APPROVAL_REQUIRED`) with exactly two business bindings: required Closure Decision (backend options ACCEPT/DECLINE) and optional Closure Remarks (required only for DECLINE, maximum 2,000 characters). Form submission answers are not stored as generic form answers; the dedicated approval API records the decision in the existing closure approval table and append-only defect event.

The configured closure route is separate from initial Reviewer routing. V35 adds a tenant-owned closure-team reference and allows the existing maintenance-team master to classify a team as CLOSURE. No default route or permission is automatically assigned. A caller needs the existing APPROVE permission, active organization membership, and active membership in the configured active CLOSURE or REVIEWER team. V36 exposes closure-stage defects in the existing shared Reviewer queue for eligible closure reviewers. Closure decisions are accepted only at APPROVAL_REQUIRED, under a row lock, using the exact currently published Galley closure form/version. ACCEPT moves APPROVAL_REQUIRED → CLOSED. DECLINE requires a reason and moves APPROVAL_REQUIRED → IN_PROGRESS by creating a new corrective-action row for the prior maintenance assignment; completed action rows, submissions, evidence, and past decisions remain intact. Generic area-only form resolution rejects closure forms; use the defect-scoped resolver so case status and routing can be checked.

